            "review_title": "Review at Taj Mahal Restaurant",
            "review_text": "koolman3\nLeeds, United Kingdom2268 contributions\n1\nLovely place\nNov 2019\nThis is a fantastic place tucked away in a tiny street around backpacker area; its not easy to find. There is a little alley just off the main road; you can see the restaurant sign from the road if you look hard enough. But when you do find it you will get very good food at reasonable prices. It turned out that the owner Mr Zaman was from the same part of the world where I hail from - what a small world! The food is very good and close to being authentic with the main dishes being above average. The nans and rotis were tasty as were the drinks. The vegetable dishes, especially Okra, were to die for. We really enjoyed the meal and had a good chat with the owner afterwards. Highly recommended.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 17, 2020",
